Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-18-2000||03:13 PM||||Does anyone know of anyone who makes tinted covers for fiero taillights and if so please tell me who. or is there another car that will work for tail light covers?<P>Thanks <BR>Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||12-18-2000||03:52 PM||||You can spend about $7 and do it yourself. Summit Racing makes a spray tint. There is a pic of my GT with tinted taillights that I did myself in one day and also a link to summit racing. The hardest part is getting the old glue off the taillight and re-securing it.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||12-18-2000||08:09 PM||||fiero lisa do you have an exact link of the item or what it is exactly called and is the spray go on the inside???<P><BR>thanks<BR>Dan<P><P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||12-18-2000||08:21 PM||||Dan,<BR>Hmm I can't remember exactly what the spray it called. But you can buy it at Summitracing (www.Summitracing.com). It does spray on the inside and it turns out real nice, only downside is, it is illegal at night to have tinted taillight covers and of course these are not removable.<BR>But it took me about 30 minutes to do each tailight, a night to dry, then just bought some adhesive at auto zone to re-attach the taillights, they WILL fall off if you don't re-glue (Jonathan [slammed fiero] had his fall off somewhere on the road and had to pay $130 for a new taillight)<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mi Junk||12-18-2000||09:15 PM||||The stuff is called Nite Shades if a remember correctly. It comes in a silver can. It works real well, but make sure you have GOOD vent.||||reg||12
Z||000005||FieroLisa||12-18-2000||09:24 PM||||Yep, thats the stuff- I just did mine out in a parking lot- but that stuff will kill ya if you try to do it anywhere without vents- talk about fumes!<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
